skills/humanizer
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived from the "humanizer" Claude Code skill by blader.
  Source:  https://github.com/blader/humanizer
  License: MIT

The pattern catalogue is based on Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing" guide,
maintained by WikiProject AI Cleanup.
  Source:  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC BY-SA)

Last synced against upstream v3.0.0 (commit 9862685, 2026-09-06) on 2026-09-12.

Modifications by The Flywheel: added an optional VOICE.md / _VOICE.md
voice-profile loading step (Step 0, nearest-ancestor resolution with section
cascade) so the skill can match a per-project editorial voice; added a
personality-and-soul section; and added patterns upstream does not carry
(uniform sentence length, transition-word overload, elegant variation, false
ranges, abstract verb inflation, filler phrases). The VOICE.md mechanism is
generic and carries no external dependency.

Adopted from upstream v3.0.0: the severity model (act-on-sight vs "weak
alone"), the structure-before-vocabulary A-E grouping, the fact guardrail, the
three output modes, the prompt-injection line, the "when not to act"
exemptions, and patterns 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 10, 11, 17, 30 and 31.

